# xv6-riscv Medical Device Security Extension

This project extends the xv6-riscv operating system by adding a complete security system designed for a simulated medical wearable device, specifically an insulin pump environment.

The goal of the project was to transform xv6 from a simple teaching operating system into a more secure system capable of handling authentication, authorization, and auditing completely inside the kernel.

The entire security model runs in Ring 0 (kernel mode), meaning user programs cannot bypass or manipulate the protection mechanisms directly.

The project was developed for the Operating Systems Security course at Modern Academy for Engineering & Technology (MAET).

